I agree in the "may be". As long as many boulders are still present in
that place I wouldn't ever do that. Later, if only few boulders are left
it *may* be a solution; the percentage of inappropriate locations is
still very high. And one should only do that if there are appropriate
spare boulders to move still present to fill the remaining traps.

Some statistics... (I made some area distinctions)
  bad  - locations where boulders cannot be used to fill remaining traps
  trap - initial trap locations (already filled traps will count as bad)
  cond - free space in the "first part" of the sokoban maze, quality of
         target location depending on other boulders still present
  okay - free space in the "second part" of the sokoban maze (room with
         up-stairs [or zoo in soko1], boulders unusable to fill traps)

